WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.213
Waves need a rhythm.

2
00:00:01.213 --> 00:00:04.155
Users hear about the change
about two months ahead,

3
00:00:04.155 --> 00:00:08.150
get their training a month out, and
get reminders in the last two weeks.

4
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.170
Then, before anything is enforced, there's
a readiness check on three numbers:

5
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.198
how many users registered
a new sign-in method,

6
00:00:16.198 --> 00:00:19.863
how many finished training,
and how busy the help desk is.

7
00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.925
When tickets climb, the
guidance is to slow down.

8
00:00:22.925 --> 00:00:25.533
The wave owner, identity engineering,

9
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:28.813
makes the go or no-go, with
training now part of it.

10
00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:34.062
And the rule is simple: a wave that isn't
ready moves its date, not its threshold.

11
00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:36.050
Next, who owns all of this.
